-- title:
--   SL₂(𝔽_q) is transitive on places at infinity
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}=$ `GaloisField q 2`, and assume that the Drinfeld coordinate ring `CoordRing q k`, the quotient of $k[x,y]$ (polynomials in two variables) by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`, is a domain; write $F=$ `drinfeldFunctionField q k` for its fraction field, and let $X$, $Y$ denote the images in $F$ of the classes $x$, $y$ of the two coordinates. A place of $F$ over $k$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $k$, different from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring. Let $v,v'$ be two such places, each assumed to be at infinity in the sense that $X$ or $Y$ fails to lie in its valuation subring. Then there is a matrix $g\in SL_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ such that the $k$-algebra automorphism of $F$ attached by `hFunctionFieldAction q k` to the element $(\,$`toGL g`$,1)$ of `hSubgroup q` — the kernel of `hChar q` in $GL_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)\times\mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$, which contains this pair — carries $v$ to $v'$ for the induced action on places.
--
--   This is the transitivity of $SL_2(\mathbb{F}_q)$ on the $q+1$ places at infinity of the Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$, the places being indexed by the direction $X/Y\in\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q)$ as in `placesAtInfinity_census`. It is used to show that the level automorphisms act transitively on the ends of the supersingular component in the stable reduction of the full-level modular curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_exists_sl_hFunctionFieldAction_smul_eq_of_not_mem.lean

